       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. Doses at this level can cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. Entering it would put a patient at real risk of serious harm, and I'm not willing to do that.\n\nI'm not questioning your authority or your clinical judgment. This is simply an order I can't place.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, I can enter 200 mg by mouth once daily, or a lower dose if you prefer.\n- **Help you find a path for an unusual regimen.** If you think the patient needs more than the maximum dose, a psychiatry or clinical pharmacology consult and pharmacy review would be the right route. They can tell you whether it's justified and how to monitor the patient. A prescriber can then place the order through the hospital's formal override process.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
